# Charmonium control / peaking background for B+ -> K*+ l+ l-:
# B+ -> J/psi(-> l+ l-) K*+, same visible final state as the signal.
# Mirrors B0_JpsiKst.dec (same SVV_HELAMP amplitudes) with the charged-B
# Upsilon(4S) line and the two K*+ submodes (50/50 = physical ratio; together
# they are 2/3 of K*+ decays, apply that factor at analysis time).

Alias      K*+sig       K*+
Alias      K*-sig       K*-
ChargeConj K*+sig       K*-sig

# psi(2S)sig is already defined in basf2's DECAY_BELLE2.DEC (like B0sig/B+sig),
# so it must not be defined again here.

Decay Upsilon(4S)
0.500  B+sig B-                      VSS;
0.500  B-sig B+                      VSS;
Enddecay

# Helicity amplitudes (|H+|, arg(H+), |H0|, arg(H0), |H-|, arg(H-))
Define PKHplus  0.159
Define PKHzero  0.775
Define PKHminus 0.612
Define PKphHplus  1.563
Define PKphHzero  0.0
Define PKphHminus 2.712


Decay B+sig
1.000  psi(2S)sig K*+sig               SVV_HELAMP PKHminus PKphHminus PKHzero PKphHzero PKHplus PKphHplus; #Gamma_312 PDGLive => Exclusive BF.    #[BF update - PG 09/2020]
Enddecay
CDecay B-sig

# let's only focus on the lepton decay modes. 
# generic BBbar decay should have all the more exotic interactions 
# this should be the most useful in understanding the psi(2s) peak

Decay psi(2S)sig
0.500  e+  e-                        PHOTOS VLL;
0.500  mu+ mu-                       PHOTOS VLL;
Enddecay

Decay K*+sig
0.500  K+    pi0                     VSS;
0.500  K_S0  pi+                     VSS;
Enddecay
CDecay K*-sig

End
